.TH "PB-SESSION-UNSHARE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-session-unshare - End sharing while preserving the owner's terminal


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb session unshare <session-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
End sharing while preserving the owner's terminal

.PP
End sharing for one session while preserving the owner's terminal and history. Existing participants lose the shared grant according to the resulting authorization state.

.PP
Terminal sessions persist independently of a single connection and can be reattached after a disconnect. Sharing grants explicit access to a named session. Closing, deleting, and removing a participant have different effects; inspect the selected session before acting.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unshare

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-session(1)\fP
